Here's an example of how you can create a clickable SVG icon that appears on the right side of an input field:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <style>
        .container {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 10px;
            margin: 20px;
        }

        input {
            padding: 8px;
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            border-radius: 4px;
            flex-grow: 1;
        }

        .icon-container {
            position: relative;
            width: 24px;
            height: 24px;
        }

        .icon-container svg {
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        .icon-container:hover svg {
            transform: scale(1.1);
        }

        .lens {
            position: absolute;
            top: 50%;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <input type="text" id="searchInput" placeholder="Enter something...">
        <div class="icon-container">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <defs>
                    <rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="20" rx="1" fill="transparent"/>
                    <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4" fill="transparent"/>
                </defs>
            </svg>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        document.querySelector('.icon-container svg').addEventListener('click', function() {
            // You can call your function here
            console.log('Icon clicked!');
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

